The Contractor shall respond to service calls (requests) and initiate corrective actions and identify any repair requirements during normal working hours. The Contractor shall immediately respond to emergency service calls at all times. The Government may
 
transmit work orders to the Contractor for service call or emergency service call orally, by email, by creation of a work order by a Government employee or representative, or by generating an automated work order. The Contractor shall respond according to
 specified service response times.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid6503332\charrsid15296154 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 (b)\tab}
Emergency service is such urgent action required due to facility structural or equipment failure situations that threatens personnel safety and/or a wide scale threat to operations of the facility, and/or a threat of s
ignificant damage to the facility itself, and/or a situation that threatens extensive repairs to the facility with high dollar cost to repair, or any work considered by the CO or their designee to be of an emergency nature. The Contractor shall respond to
 
emergency service call immediately (within the shortest possible time consistent with the mechanic's location). Only those actions necessary to mitigate the emergency must be accomplished on the initial response. If additional work is required to restore 
c
omplete functionality, a lower priority work requirement will be created and executed in a time and manner consistent with requirements of similar scope and nature. The Contractor shall remain on the job until the emergency situation has been secured and 
adequate temporary repairs have been made. The approved CMMS system will be utilized for documentation after the call is received and a response dispatched. Permanent repair shall be governed by the repairs provisions in this document.
