\par Computer equipment loads, or other electronic equipment load,
 must be wired and connected to the circuit breaker panels that are specifically installed and designed for this equipment. Color-coded wiring shall be used for all 3 phases and shall be consistent throughout the wiring systems. When wires are shifted fro
m one phase to another, colored tape shall be used to identify the wires' new phase and color coded near its termination points.
\par 
\par Colors for the automated equipment wiring shall be red, black and blue for the 3 phases, white and gray for neutral and green f
or ground, green with yellow stripe for isolated ground.  Neutral wires, see NEC 210-5 (a). Separate bus bars shall be used for isolated and bonded ground wiring.
