\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid9317458 (1) During the period of performance of this contract, the Government will issue written task orders in accordance with the procedures as set forth herein. The Government will award firm fixed price or l
abor hour task orders against this Contract. Task order prices will be based on rates that do not exceed the contract fixed hourly rates for each labor category identified in the contract. 
\par \~\~(2) The Contractor will not be reimbursed for any expenses incurred that do not comply with these task ordering procedures or expenses that exceed the task order ceiling without the express written consent of the Contracting Officer. 
\par \~\~(3) No individual task order may authorize the Contractor to incur expenses that are not in accordance with the limitations set forth elsewhere in the contract
\par \~\~(4) The Government is obligated only to the extent of authorized purchases (Task Orders) actually made under the Contract. The Government will identify the period of performance in each task order. 
\par \~\~(5) The Government shall issue task orders only by fax or electronically.
\par (b) Ordering
\par \~\~(1) The Contracting Officer will issue a request for task order proposal (RFTOP) to the Contractor. In response, the Contractor shall provide a task order proposal (TOP) that contains the Contractor\rquote 
s proposed price to perform the Statement of Work. Any additional information that may be required by the Government will be indicated in the RFTOP.
\par \~\~(2) All SSA Contracting Officers may place orders against this contract up to their individual delegated purchase authority. 
\par \~\~(3) Funds will be obligated at the time the CO places a task order.
\par \~\~(4) Frequency of ordering: SSA COs will order services on an as needed basis and as funds are available.
\par (c) Task Order Proposal (TOP) 
\par \~\~(1) The Contractor\rquote s proposal shall contain the Contractor\rquote s proposed price to perform the work detailed in the RFTOP\rquote s Statement of Work. Below is a list of areas that the TOP shall address:
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \s129 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid9317458 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 (i)\tab}}\pard \ltrpar\s129\ql \li630\ri0\sb240\sa240\widctlpar
\tx990\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls79\adjustright\rin0\lin630\itap0\pararsid9317458 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid9317458 Labor\line The TOP shall include a
