the prices will be based on rates that do not exceed the contract fixed hourly rates for each labor category identified in the contract. The Government will use the fixed labor rates current at the time of issuance of the task order and not necessarily th
ose in effect when the work is performed. 
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \s129 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid9317458 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 (ii)\tab}Parts and Materials\line 
If parts or materials are required for a project, the Government may provide the parts and materials or the Contractor may be asked to provide the parts and materials. Parts and materials s
hall be priced at estimated actual cost marked up by the agreed upon fees. 
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \s129 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid9317458 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 (iii)\tab} Cost Documentation\line 
If the Contractor provides the parts and materials, or if work is subcontracted, the Contractor shall furnish on request, copies of invoices, vendor quotes, or receipts, either with the TOP or as substantiating documentation with the Contractor\rquote 
s invoice after completion of work.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \s129 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid9317458 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 (iv)\tab} Competitive Quotes\line If a single part or component, or a single type (line item) of parts, components, and materials for a pr
oject is anticipated to equal or exceed the micro-purchase threshold, the CO or COTR, at their discretion, may require that the Contractor obtain three quotes from suppliers and include documentation of these quotes with the TOP. If subcontract work is an
ticipated to exceed the micro-purchase threshold, the CO or COTR, at their discretion may require that the Contractor obtain three quotes from potential subcontractors and include documentation of these quotes with the TOP. 
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\ltrpar \s129 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid9317458 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 (v)\tab}Assumptions\line The TOP may include any assumptions on the Contractor\rquote s part used in developing the TOP and costs. 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\s129\ql \li0\ri0\sb240\sa240\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid9317458 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid9317458  (d) Task Order Proposal Response Time
\par Unless otherwise specified the Contractor shall respond to the Government\rquote s RFTOP within 7 calendar days after receipt of the request. The Contractor may request additional response time; the Government may or may not grant an extension.
\par (e) Task Order Evaluation
\par At the task order level, the Government will evaluate the proposed prices, the labor mix, and the level of effort to determine if the task order proposal is reasonable for the required work and reflects a clear understanding of the requirements. 
\par (f) Task Order Modifications
\par \~\~(1) Changes within the scope of the task order shall require a modification. Modifications may include, but are not limited to, the Statement of Work, the duration of a task order, and/or funding.
\par \~\~(2) The COTR, SSA task manager (if applicable), and Contractor shall discuss the changes. The CO will then request that the Contractor provide a
 revised price proposal based on the recommended changes. The COTR will then review the modification proposal and send a recommendation to the CO. Once approved by the CO, the CO will issue a task order modification to the Contractor. The Contractor may n
ot begin performance on the modification until the CO provides approval.
